        "title": "feat(daytona): add coordinator-managed leases",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a provider-neutral Daytona REST adapter to the Cloudflare coordinator\n- provision, resolve, refresh SSH access for, and release Daytona sandboxes through brokered leases\n- add CLI targeting, secret redaction, readiness reporting, configuration, docs, and release notes\n- omit implicit architecture for Daytona and use a snapshot-native SSH readiness probe\n\n## Why\n\nDaytona was available only as a direct provider. This makes it usable through the shared Crabbox coordinator while keeping the API key coordinator-managed and short-lived SSH access tokens out of list and portal output.\n\n## Configuration\n\nProduction requires the `DAYTONA_CRABBOX_KEY` Worker secret. It has been installed on `crabbox-coordinator`; no secret value is stored in this branch.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli ./internal/providers/daytona ./internal/providers/all ./internal/providers/tart`\n- `go build -trimpath -o bin/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox`\n- `npm run format:check --prefix worker`\n- `npm run lint --prefix worker`\n- `npm run check --prefix worker`\n- `npm test --prefix worker` (875 passed, 3 skipped)\n- `npm run build --prefix worker`\n- autoreview: clean, no actionable findings\n- deployed Worker version `58e4f08f-0c63-4ffb-b075-f46786769896`\n- live Daytona smoke: run `run_38dc2e178129`, lease `cbx_88a4a6a30cec`, exit 0, release confirmed, zero matching Daytona sandboxes after cleanup",
